<title>UK: EIB adds 200 bln lire to 6.20 pct March 2002 bond. [CORRECTED 12:58 GMT]</title>
<headline>EIB adds 200 bln lire to 6.20 pct March 2002 bond. [CORRECTED 12:58 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following fungible bond was</p>
<p>announced by joint lead managers IMI Lux amd Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT   *200 BLN LIRE  COUPON     6.20	MATURITY    05.MAR.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  102.202   PAY DATE    10.SEP.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> NOTES     *FUNGIBLE WITH OUTSTANDING 900 BLN LIRE DEAL.</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   SYANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.50     SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>(Corrects MGT/UND to 0.50 from 0.625)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
